This project analyzed the performance of five customer acquisition channels — Facebook, Email, Google Ads, Instagram, and Twitter — to identify the most profitable source. I:

Cleaned and transformed raw marketing data to ensure accuracy.

Segmented performance by acquisition channel for direct comparisons.

Calculated key metrics, including conversion rate and Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC), to assess cost-effectiveness.

Determined Google Ads as the top-performing channel, achieving the best balance of low CAC and high conversion rates.

Designed clear, interactive visualizations to communicate insights to the marketing team, enabling data-driven budget allocation.
